ent-OrbitraMechRipleyAbandoned = abandoned Ripley APLU
    .desc = Ash cakes the loader's knee joints. A charred length of cable hangs from the drive housing.
ent-OrbitraMechMiningDrill = quick-release mining drill
    .desc = A rock drill with a hand grip and a quick-release bracket for an exosuit tool mount.

orbitra-lavaland-ripley-drive-broken = The drive is locked. Fit a charged power cell in the maintenance panel, then splice the drive lead with one length of LV cable.
orbitra-lavaland-ripley-strip = The equipment release still works. Open the control panel to detach the mining drill.
orbitra-lavaland-ripley-drive-repaired = A fresh splice bridges the drive lead. With a charged cell installed, the loader can walk again.
orbitra-lavaland-ripley-repair-success = The drive clicks into gear and the Ripley rises to its feet.
orbitra-lavaland-ripley-needs-power = The drive needs a charged power cell for the test.
